PSIRING  Program

INSTALLATION  NOTES

There are some changes to the way files may be installed in ver 1.06.

There are four main files for Psiring: PSIRING.OPA, METHODS.DBF, PSIRING.ICN and RINGHELP.DBF. The default location for the .DBF and ICN files is the M:\APP\ directory.

PSIRING.OPA should be located in an \APP\ directory on any drive. If Psiring cannot find the dbf files in m:\app it looks in m:\opd\ for the config.rng file. If it does not find this file then it brings up the file location dialog which allows you to specify where the Methods, Help and Icon files are named and located. 

You can change these settings usng the File (Psion-F) menu selection. Your choices are saved in the config.rng file abovementioned.

METHODS is the file you will want to update with your own methods. You can either open the main file as a data application or copy it to a DAT directory and copy it to the program directory whenever the file is changed, overwriting the older working version of the file which is already there. This will avoid the risk of a 'file open' error when Psiring tries to access the file.
